# AI workflow

Canonical instructions: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Read it before any code.

## Workflow at a glance

1. Classify the change Level 0–3 per [`docs/feature-workflow.md`](../../docs/feature-workflow.md#complexity-levels). Check [always-approval triggers](../../docs/feature-workflow.md#always-approval-triggers).
2. For Level 2+, load durable context: `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/coding-conventions.md`, `docs/patterns.md`, relevant `docs/domains/*`.
3. Plan via the `plan` skill — scaffolds a Draft task in `docs/tasks/` (gitignored). Approve flips Status to Approved.
4. Build via the `implement` skill — refuses non-Approved tasks. Verifies, distills into `docs/domains/<domain>.md`, deletes the task file, commits.

## Skills

Available in `.cursor/skills/`:

- `describe-project` — one-time docs bootstrap (README, architecture.md, AGENTS.md project block).
- `plan` — plan/refine/approve. No code.
- `implement` — execute Approved tasks or Level 0/1 fixes.

Invoke by describing the task naturally (e.g. "plan this bug", "implement add_import_pipeline"); the agent matches against each skill's `description:` frontmatter.

## Hard rules

- Never silently hit an always-approval trigger.
- Task files are gitignored scratch — never commit them.
- Distill durable knowledge into `docs/domains/<domain>.md` on close-out; delete the task file.
- Use Conventional Commits; one logical change per commit; never `--no-verify`.
